  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>OF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;molecule consider the following:<br />(A) Number of lone pairs on oxygen is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.<br />(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FOF</mi></math>&nbsp;angle is less than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>104</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.<br />(C) Oxidation state of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.<br />(D) Molecule is bent &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&#39; shaped.<br />(E) Molecular geometry is linear.</p><p><strong>Correct</strong> options are:</p>"
  },
